      "math_academy_id": "e-4690",
      "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14118591/assets/cbbe84f508fe2b9c97160f8e1389e88b8c7ecf2e1681b4a9a612a025796d4627.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$",
